meta {
  name: Create embedding
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/v1/embeddings
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "model": "{{model}}",
    "input": "Say PONG"
  }
}

vars:post-response {
  embeddingId: res.body.id
}

docs {
  Queued, like every call that costs the upstream real compute. Answers
  `202` with an `id`, a `poll_url` and the `queue` block; collect the
  vectors with **Collect embedding**.

  It used to answer inline. An indexing run posts tens of thousands of
  batches, and answering them inline let all of them hit the backend at
  once — queued, the workers run them one at a time and a failed batch
  retries on its own budget instead of failing in the caller's hand.

  Anthropic has no embeddings API; a gateway pointed at one records the
  entry as failed with Anthropic's own `404`.
}
